

# ---- GLOBAL RULES FOR PROJECT ----

# Folder responsibility
/backend is backend logic only, implemented in Flask
/backend/crew holds all CrewAI logic (agents, supervisor, tasks, and tools)
/backend/vector is responsible for the RAG pipeline (embeddings + vector DB)
/backend/db contains database models and persistence helpers
/streamlit is the user interface and must never contain backend logic

# API boundaries
Flask exposes JSON endpoints only
Streamlit calls Flask through /streamlit/api_client.py
Streamlit must never connect directly to CrewAI or to the database

# CrewAI architecture
supervisor.py orchestrates other agents and tasks
agents.py defines agent behaviors but NO business logic
tools.py defines all non-LLM functions (database ops, vector DB retrieval, webhook POSTs)
crew.py wires everything together for CrewAI

# RAG rules
rag.py must handle:
    - PDF ingestion
    - text chunking
    - embeddings
    - vector DB search
Agents must never call embeddings or vector DB directly; they must call a tool

# Database
models.py defines schema only
plan_ops.py handles persistence logic only

# Coding style
- Use docstrings and type hints
- Functions must be small and single-responsibility
- Agents return structured dicts/JSON, not free-form text

# Safety against project corruption
Cursor must NOT:
- move folders
- merge backend + frontend code
- delete or replace entire files unless explicitly asked
- embed API keys directly in code
